<header><p class="enc-kicker">Historical factor</p><h1 class="enc-title">Depopulation and demographic collapse</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Depopulation and demographic collapse refers to sharp falls in population caused by epidemic disease, war, famine or <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slave-raiding">slave raiding</a>, which undermined the economic and military base of states. Examples include the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aztec-empire">Aztec Empire</a>, devastated by epidemics after the Spanish conquest, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk-sultanate">Mamluk Sultanate</a> after recurring plague, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuan-dynasty">Yuan Dynasty</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timurid-empire">Timurid Empire</a>.</p></div>
